  "usage_note": "When **a bunch of** means *a lot of*, the verb agrees with the noun after it: plural before a plural noun (*A bunch of kids were playing outside*), singular before an uncountable noun (*A bunch of work is still waiting*). When it means one tied group, the verb is singular: *A bunch of flowers was on the table*.",
